-- title:
--   Vanishing corrected angular residual limit
-- statement:
--   In the fixed pure five-dimensional Einstein-Maxwell equal-spin radial setting with Lambda=0, no Chern-Simons term, RN anchor (3,1,3/2), and exterior R>3, for every real j and each fixed R>3, [ellFun(fE,mE,N0,wE,pE,aE)(R)+2*epsilon*j]/epsilon^3 tends to zero as epsilon tends to zero through nonzero values.
--
--   Scope: This node asserts exactly its displayed Lean statement with every hypothesis retained. Its role in Atlas VIII does not narrow more general supporting results to the fixed RN anchor. The project does not establish a finite-rotation spacetime, extension of such a spacetime through a horizon, or a normalized physical magnetic moment. Radial endpoint extensions proved in the displayed theorems are retained. No literature priority is claimed.
-- source:
--   Project formalization, frozen source commit 323deba9a80475cfd477eb35bd415aa9d2dc18ff; Atlas/EinsteinMaxwell/ES5/KerrSchild/VIII09R/Roots.lean, lines 54-72; SHA-256 6012a6eae0747e077a3d2be754d9efddc2700103e5bc76cd1d10df2d3033db65. No public repository URL is claimed. Background radial equations: Froeb et al., EPJC 82 (2022) 215, https://arxiv.org/abs/2112.13266 (background citation, not a claimed source of this exact formal theorem).

